  "body": {
    "id": "prop:strict-witness-exact-frontier-gap",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For \\(\\mathsf I_*\\), the coordinatewise minimum-variance vectors are\n\\[\n (v_{\\mathrm{nested},(1,0)},v_{\\mathrm{nested},(1,1)})\n =\\left(\\frac43,\\frac3{200}\\right),\n \\qquad\n (v_{\\mathrm{deep},(1,0)},v_{\\mathrm{deep},(1,1)})\n =\\left(\\frac32,\\frac3{200}\\right).\n\\]\nThe exact frontiers are the unique positive roots of\n\\[\n \\left\\{2\\Phi(R/\\sqrt{v_{s,(1,0)}})-1\\right\\}\n \\left\\{2\\Phi(R/\\sqrt{3/200})-1\\right\\}=\\frac{19}{20}.\n\\]\nSince \\(4/3<3/2\\), \\texttt{thm:disjoint-diagonal-exact-frontier} gives \\(W_{\\mathrm{nested}}<W_{\\mathrm{deep}}\\). Thus the witness has a strict exact-frontier gain as well as the strict fixed-Bonferroni SOCP gain in \\texttt{prop:strict-witness-gap}.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "WitnessInst",
      "vse",
      "Ws",
      "alpha",
      "SigmaQ",
      "RQ",
      "L",
      "delta"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:strict-witness-instance",
      "def:support-rule-row-cells",
      "def:coordinate-minimum-variance",
      "prop:strict-witness-gap",
      "thm:disjoint-diagonal-exact-frontier"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "The definition of \\(\\mathsf I_*\\) gives \\(\\mathcal E=\\{(1,0),(1,1)\\}\\), so\nthe index set is nonempty.  Under nested support the eligible row-cell sets\nare\n\\[\n \\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{nested}}_{(1,0)}\n =\\{(1,2),(2,2),(3,2),(4,2)\\},\n \\qquad\n \\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{nested}}_{(1,1)}\n =\\{(1,3),(3,3),(4,3)\\}.\n\\]\nUnder deep support the first set loses only \\((2,2)\\), while the second set is\nunchanged.  In either rule, the two sets are disjoint because their calendar\ntimes differ.  Moreover, \\(\\Sigma_Q=R_Q^{\\top}R_Q\\) is diagonal, with\ndiagonal entries one on the time-\\(2\\) cells and \\(1/100\\) on the time-\\(3\\)\ncells; its smallest and largest eigenvalues are therefore respectively\n\\(1/100\\) and one.  The remaining subclass conditions\n\\(L=\\delta=0\\) are part of the witness definition.\n\nThe variance minimizations in \\texttt{prop:strict-witness-gap}, together with\n\\texttt{def:coordinate-minimum-variance}, give\n\\[\n v_{\\mathrm{nested},(1,0)}=\\frac43,\n \\quad v_{\\mathrm{deep},(1,0)}=\\frac32,\n \\quad\n v_{\\mathrm{nested},(1,1)}=v_{\\mathrm{deep},(1,1)}=\\frac3{200}. \\tag{16}\n\\]\nThe hypotheses of \\texttt{thm:disjoint-diagonal-exact-frontier} now hold for\nboth rules.  Substituting (16) and \\(1-\\alpha=19/20\\) in (8) gives the two\ndisplayed root equations.  Since \\(4/3<3/2\\), the strict-coordinate conclusion\nof that theorem proves\n\\[\n W_{\\mathrm{nested}}<W_{\\mathrm{deep}}. \\tag{17}\n\\]",
    "justification": "The outward-rounded intervals certify material strictness for the actual robust-width target rather than inferring it from the surrogate SOCP gap.",
    "gap": "No claim is made that these exact widths equal the output of the Ben-Michael--Feller--Rothstein estimator.",
    "consumer": "The intervals are deterministic regression targets for independent-Gaussian calibration in \\(\\texttt{scpi}\\) and \\(\\texttt{augsynth::multisynth}\\).",
